  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Tormach post's safe retract `G53 G0 Z0` assumed machine Z0 is the top of Z travel. That holds on a Tormach, but on a LinuxCNC machine homed with Z0 at the bottom it rapids down into the part (reported on #435).\n\n- **Machine file:** an optional `safe_retract` on the linear Z part gives the retract Z in MACHINE coordinates, in the file's length unit (scaled like travel). Zero counts as a stated value. A non-number, or the key on any other axis, refuses the file and names the axis. The mirror carries it as `safeRetractZ` (mm). The script sees `machine.safeRetractZ` (or `null`) and `machine.model`, the model name through either door (app mirror or CLI raw file).\n- **Shipped machines:** every Tormach `.mch` states `0.0`. So do `vmc.mch`, `tilthead.mch` and the default `3axis-vmc.mch` (`\"safeRetractZ\": 0.0`).\n- **tormach.cps:**\n  - A stated safe Z posts `G53 G0 Z<that>`.\n  - With no machine, or a model named \"Tormach...\" that states no safe Z, the output is unchanged (`G53 G0 Z0` + `G30`).\n  - Any other machine that states no safe Z gets one counted `message()` that names the machine and the key, and no retract line is written. The in-app gate blocks the write.\n  - A non-zero safe Z drops `G30`, because an unset G30 position on LinuxCNC is the machine origin. The header then says `(SAFE RETRACT G53 Z<v> - STATED BY THE MACHINE)`.\n- **Docs:** `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`, `assets/posts/AGENTS.md`, `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md`, and the decision file `docs/decisions/495-safe-retract.md` (alternatives considered, plus notes on the other posts).\n\n## How tested\n\nNew `crates/app/tests/tormach_safe_retract.rs`:\n- `the_shipped_tormach_machines_post_byte_identical`: every library Tormach posts byte-identical with and without the key. A null machine and the default VMC also keep `G53 G0 Z0` / `G30`.\n- `a_stated_safe_z_posts_that_z`: covers the mirror and the raw door. An inch file scales, there is no G30, and the header comment is written.\n- `a_non_tormach_machine_without_a_safe_z_is_refused_by_name`: covers the mirror and the raw door, and checks that a Tormach-named file without the key still posts Z0.\n- `a_garbled_safe_retract_refuses_the_file`\n\nGate: `cargo test -p camcraft-post` (all), plus 64 camcraft-app suites touching posts and machines, all green. These include conformance (every golden byte-exact), tormach_post, tormach_machines, machine, machine_library, posting, fanuc_post, inverted_post, program_comments, project_roundtrip, wear_comp and control_comp. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real machine cut and no Hub sim.\n- The UI machine sheet does not show the new key yet.\n- The CLI `post` binary was not smoke-run by hand. Its raw-door path is covered by the tests.\n- Behaviour change: a document saved before this change with a mounted non-Tormach machine (for example the library \"VMC 3-axis\") stores that machine without the key. Posting it through the Tormach post is now refused by name until the machine is re-mounted.\n\nChangelog: Tormach post retracts to the machine's stated safe Z (`safe_retract`, machine coordinates) and refuses a non-Tormach machine that states none, instead of assuming machine Z0 is the top of travel\n\nFixes #495\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
